# Upload to Cloud — Explicit Opt-In

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:plotly_ex, "~> 0.3"},
  {:kino, "~> 0.18"}
])
```

## Choose whether to offer cloud upload

Plotly.js v4 removed Edit in Chart Studio and its `showEditInChartStudio`
configuration. Upload to Cloud is a separate button: plotly_ex hides it by
default. This example deliberately enables it with `showSendToCloud: true`.
Rendering the chart does not upload data; clicking the button starts the
external cloud workflow.

```elixir
alias Plotly.{Figure, Scatter}

Figure.new(config: %{showSendToCloud: true})
|> Figure.add_trace(Scatter.new(x: [1, 2, 3], y: [2, 5, 3], mode: "lines+markers"))
|> Figure.update_layout(title: "Upload to Cloud is explicitly enabled here")
|> Plotly.show()
```
